    "notes": "Announced July 2025 by Crusoe and Tallgrass as Project Jade (1.8 GW, scalable to 10 GW). Laramie County approved the campus and the Tallgrass gas plant in January 2026 (POWER Magazine: https://www.powermag.com/wyoming-approves-data-center-campus-that-includes-2-7-gw-of-new-natural-gas-fired-generation/). In June 2026 Crusoe paused work at its customer's request; Google subsidiary Jupiter Star Holdings took over and filed a site-plan amendment June 30, 2026 (county hearing Aug. 13, 2026). Completion planned 2031. Total cost figures (about $50B) seen only in secondary sources, not recorded. Black Hills confirmed the Google agreements in its Oct 6, 2026 8-K (LPCSA + GFA, effective Sept 30, 2026). Google gave Black Hills $399M of refundable advances for long-lead equipment under an April 22, 2026 generation reservation agreement (customer described there as a 1.8 GW data center)."
